        <h3>"Joy to the World" Started the Decade's Party</h3>
        <p>Three Dog Night's "Joy to the World" reached number one in the spring of 1971.</p>
        <p>It stayed there for six straight weeks.</p>
        <p>It then finished as Billboard's top single of the year.</p>
        <p>The full story is on the <a href="/blog/songs/joy-to-the-world-three-dog-night/">Joy to the World</a> page.</p>

        <h3>"Le Freak" Took Six Weeks in Three Stretches</h3>
        <p>Chic's "Le Freak" first reached number one on December 9, 1978.</p>
        <p>It lost the top spot, came back, lost it again and returned for a last run that ended on February 3, 1979.</p>
        <p>Barbra Streisand and Neil Diamond's "You Don't Bring Me Flowers" and the Bee Gees' "Too Much Heaven" took the weeks in between.</p>
        <p>Added up, that is six weeks at number one, tied for the most on this list.</p>

        <h2 id="sound">The Sound of the List: Disco, Funk and Beyond</h2>
        <p>This site tags every song in its data with a genre.</p>
        <p>Counting the {{N}} songs by that tag shows how much of the list is disco.</p>

