        <h3>{{TOP_YEAR}} Is the Peak Year</h3>
        <p>Five songs from {{TOP_YEAR}} made the list, and every one of them reached number one.</p>
        <p>That year gave us "Hooked on a Feeling," "TSOP," "The Loco-Motion," "Rock the Boat" and "Rock Your Baby."</p>
        <p>All five hit the top between April 6 and July 20, 1974.</p>

        <h3>The Decade Closes on the Dance Floor</h3>
        <p>"Le Freak" and "I Will Survive" carried the party into 1979.</p>
        <p>For the rest of the decade's chart story, start at <a href="/">Music of the 70s</a>, then see the <a href="/blog/songs/70s-number-one-hits/">70s number one hits</a> page.</p>
        <p>For the slower side of the same chart, play the <a href="/blog/songs/70s-love-songs/">70s love songs</a> list.</p>

